==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|blanquet||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|blanquette}}, from {{der|en|prv|blanqueto}}, a diminutive of {{m|oc|blanc||white}}, derived, through {{der|en|LL.|-}} and {{der|en|VL.|*blancus}}, from {{der|en|frk|*blank||gleaming, white, blinding}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*blankaz||white, bright, blinding}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bhleg-||to shine}}.<br/> Compare {{m|en|blanket}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{wikipedia|blanquette de veau}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/blɒ̃ˈkɛt/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/blɑ̃ˈkɛt/|/blɑŋˈkɛt/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛt|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[white meat]] [[stew]] in which neither the meat nor the [[sauce]] is [[browned]].
#: {{hyper|en|ragout|stew}}
#: {{hypo|en|blanquette de veau}}

